## Summary

Adds the canonical repository-backed execution specifications for CVortex Phases 06–12 and expands the original short phase prompts into bounded, reviewable, security-aware task contracts.

This PR is documentation/agent-operating-layer only. It does **not** execute Phase 06 or any later phase and does not add product code, migrations, dependencies, infrastructure or accepted architecture changes.

## Added task specifications

- `.agents/tasks/phase-06-product-data-ai-security-design.md`
- `.agents/tasks/phase-07-design-foundation.md`
- `.agents/tasks/phase-08-repository-bootstrap.md`
- `.agents/tasks/phase-09-auth-multi-user.md`
- `.agents/tasks/phase-10-career-foundation.md`
- `.agents/tasks/phase-11-vacancies-matching.md`
- `.agents/tasks/phase-12-application-package.md`

## Updated

- `.agents/tasks/README.md`
  - canonical phase-spec index;
  - short launch prompt;
  - independent review prompt;
  - EXECUTE → REVIEW → FIX → REVIEW → PASS → PR → human merge workflow;
  - explicit distinction between task-spec `status: ready` and actual project phase authorization.
- `.agents/state/STATUS.md`
  - records preparation/review of Phase 06–12 specs;
  - explicitly preserves current `NEXT = 06-product-data-ai-security-design`.

## Phase 06 changes

The large Phase 06 design prompt was retained at full design depth but adjusted to the new resource policy:

- lazy/task-specific context instead of mandatory full Phase 03–04/doc-tree reloads;
- targeted research only for real unresolved freshness-sensitive gaps;
- one-agent/sequential defaults;
- no unnecessary subagents;
- concise final report instead of repeating generated design documentation;
- full PASS/FAIL completion criteria retained;
- explicit accepted-ADR conflict handling retained;
- FACT → CLAIM → GENERATED CONTENT and STRICT Truth Guard remain mandatory;
- Runtime AI Skills remain separated from `.agents/`.

## Phase 07 expansion

Expands Design Foundation into a full task spec covering:

- canonical tokens;
- dark-first CVortex brand invariants;
- typography/spacing/radii/elevation/motion/breakpoints/layers;
