## Phase 09 expansion

Authentication + Multi-user now explicitly covers:

- invite-only registration;
- secure invitation tokens, expiry, revocation and atomic usage limits;
- optional target email;
- login/logout/session security;
- admin/user boundaries;
- reusable server-side ownership policies;
- IDOR/cross-user negative tests;
- encrypted-secret foundation;
- audit events without secret material;
- rate limits and safe errors;
- migrations/OpenAPI/frontend scope;
- no Career/Vacancy implementation.

## Phase 10 expansion

Career Foundation now explicitly enforces:

```text
SOURCE
→ PENDING Career Fact
→ HUMAN CONFIRMATION
→ CONFIRMED Career Fact
→ Claim
→ Generated Content
```

It covers:

- CareerProfile / CareerTrack / EmploymentHistory / CareerFact;
- provenance and source versions;
- safe resume import;
- deterministic parsing separated from semantic extraction;
- versioned Fact Extraction Skill;
- AI extraction can create `PENDING` only;
- human Confirm/Edit/Reject;
- Claim Registry foundation;
- STRICT Truth Guard foundation;
- upload security;
- LLM run accounting/evals;
- invariant fixtures and cross-user tests.

## Phase 11 expansion

Vacancies + Matching now covers:

- Vacancy / VacancySource / VacancySnapshot / VacancyRequirement;
- immutable/versioned raw-source preservation;
- hashing and exact duplicate handling;
- Manual/Paste ingestion baseline;
- URL ingestion only where Phase 04 evidence permits it;
- SSRF-safe fetch requirements;
- adapter boundaries;
- deterministic parsing + semantic requirement extraction;
- explainable Technical / Experience / Domain / Language / Location / Work format / Salary dimensions;
- gap analysis;
- STRONGLY_APPLY / APPLY / MAYBE / LOW_PRIORITY / SKIP;
- no fake universal ATS score;
- provenance and security/eval fixtures.

## Phase 12 expansion

Application Package now covers:

- Company / Application / ApplicationStatusHistory;
- ResumeVersion / ResumeChange;
- CoverLetter;
- Claim usage;
- Employer Memory;
- EmployerConsistencyCheck;
- deterministic READY_TO_APPLY criteria;
- explicit manual application confirmation;
- Before / After / Reason / Evidence / Risk recommendations;
- Accept / Edit / Reject;
- Truth Guard revalidation of user edits;
- confirmed employer contradictions → BLOCK or USER_RESOLUTION_REQUIRED;
- deterministic Structured Resume → DOCX → LibreOffice → PDF pipeline;
- generated-file authorization and render validation;
- no automatic employer submission;
- no invented Phase 13 when the roadmap does not define one.

## Resource-efficiency model

These task specs are intentionally stored in Git so the interactive Codex launch remains short:

```text
Execute `.agents/tasks/phase-XX-name.md`.
Follow `/AGENTS.md` and current project state.
Use one agent, sequential execution and task-relevant context only.
Complete the bounded task, update required docs/state, then STOP.
Do not proceed to the next phase.
```

Concrete provider/model names and prices are not frozen in these specs. `.agents/policies/resource-usage.md` remains authoritative for lowest-cost-capable execution and escalation only when justified.

