## Safety / routing invariants

- unchanged providers retain their exact `provider_instance_id` and healthy connection;
- changed/new providers receive a fresh identity; removed/replaced identities immediately become stale;
- queued calls are re-fenced at dispatch and never silently retarget to a replacement provider;
- already-dispatched work is not interrupted or replayed;
- stale same-instance streaming connections cannot overwrite current MCP routing authority;
- invalid runtime MCP inventories are rejected atomically; `Some([])` explicitly clears the inventory.

