This PR extends stateful single-use governance beyond the Guardian transition:
- a READY bounded implementation evaluation consumes its Guardian gate exactly once;
- blocked implementation evidence does not burn the gate and can be corrected;
- one bounded evaluation can produce only one governed application decision;
- stale evaluation context fails closed without consumption;
- an APPLY_CHANGE application decision explicitly requires MERGE_EXECUTION as the next single-use consumer;
- MERGE_EXECUTION binds one decision to one repository, PR number, exact observed head SHA, observed base SHA, successful required checks and approval evidence;
- the application decision is atomically consumed before issuing the merge execution receipt;
- replaying that decision for a second merge authorization fails closed;
- post-merge closure is bound to the merge execution hash and consumes the merge receipt exactly once only after successful measurement/provenance verification;
- blocked post-merge closure does not burn the merge receipt;
- a live `Merge Execution Gate` now audits the real GitHub repository configuration and preserves its evidence artifact.

